      "hints": [
        "Use the parallel-side vector relation to reconstruct the missing vertex.",
        "Find $\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{OB}-\\overrightarrow{OA}$, then use $\\overrightarrow{DC}=3\\overrightarrow{AB}$.",
        "Since $\\overrightarrow{DC}=\\overrightarrow{OC}-\\overrightarrow{OD}$, rearrange for $\\overrightarrow{OD}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Find the displacement vector $\\overrightarrow{AB}$:\n$$\\overrightarrow{AB} = \\overrightarrow{OB} - \\overrightarrow{OA} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 - (-1) \\\\ 3 - 2 \\\\ 1 - 3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}$$",
        "Use the given relation $\\overrightarrow{DC} = 3\\overrightarrow{AB}$:\n$$\\overrightarrow{DC} = 3\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix}$$",
        "Express the position vector of $D$ using $\\overrightarrow{DC} = \\overrightarrow{OC} - \\overrightarrow{OD}$:\n$$\\overrightarrow{OD} = \\overrightarrow{OC} - \\overrightarrow{DC} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 - 6 \\\\ 2 - 3 \\\\ -3 - (-6) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}$$",
        "State the position vector of $D$:\n$$\\overrightarrow{OD} = -4\\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j} + 3\\mathbf{k} \\quad \\left(\\text{or } \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}\\right)$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Using Position Vectors": "Identifies $\\overrightarrow{AB}=2\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}-2\\mathbf{k}$; Derives $-4\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j}+3\\mathbf{k}$; Concludes with $\\overrightarrow{OD}=-4\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j}+3\\mathbf{k}$."
        },
