      "hints": [
        "Find the perpendicular separation of the parallel sides by projecting a connecting vector perpendicular to their common direction.",
        "Let a general point $P$ on $AB$ have parameter $\\lambda$ and impose $\\overrightarrow{CP}\\cdot(2,1,-2)=0$.",
        "Solve for $\\lambda$ and calculate the length of the resulting perpendicular vector.",
        "Use the parallel side lengths $|AB|$ and $|DC|=3|AB|$ in the trapezium area formula."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Find the perpendicular distance from point $C(2, 2, -3)$ to the line through $A$ and $B$:\nLet $P$ be a point on line $AB$ with position vector $\\overrightarrow{OP} = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 + 2\\lambda \\\\ 2 + \\lambda \\\\ 3 - 2\\lambda \\end{pmatrix}$.",
        "Find the vector $\\overrightarrow{CP} = \\overrightarrow{OP} - \\overrightarrow{OC}$:\n$$\\overrightarrow{CP} = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 + 2\\lambda - 2 \\\\ 2 + \\lambda - 2 \\\\ 3 - 2\\lambda - (-3) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2\\lambda - 3 \\\\ \\lambda \\\\ 6 - 2\\lambda \\end{pmatrix}$$",
        "Set $\\overrightarrow{CP} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{AB} = 0$ for perpendicularity:\n$$2(2\\lambda - 3) + 1(\\lambda) - 2(6 - 2\\lambda) = 0$$\n$$4\\lambda - 6 + \\lambda - 12 + 4\\lambda = 0$$\n$$9\\lambda - 18 = 0 \\implies \\lambda = 2$$",
        "Calculate $\\overrightarrow{CP}$ at $\\lambda = 2$:\n$$\\overrightarrow{CP} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2(2) - 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 - 2(2) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}$$",
        "Calculate the perpendicular distance $h$ between the parallel sides:\n$$h = |\\overrightarrow{CP}| = \\sqrt{1^2 + 2^2 + 2^2} = \\sqrt{1 + 4 + 4} = \\sqrt{9} = 3$$",
        "Calculate the lengths of the two parallel sides $AB$ and $DC$:\n$$AB = |\\overrightarrow{AB}| = \\sqrt{2^2 + 1^2 + (-2)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 1 + 4} = \\sqrt{9} = 3$$\n$$DC = 3AB = 3(3) = 9$$",
        "Calculate the area of the trapezium:\n$$\\text{Area} = \\dfrac{1}{2}(AB + DC) \\times h = \\dfrac{1}{2}(3 + 9) \\times 3 = \\dfrac{1}{2}(12) \\times 3 = 18$$"
      ],
